\begin{cases}
1 & \text{if } \left\| \Omega(s_{t+1}) - \Omega(g) \right\|_2 < \epsilon \\
0 & \text{otherwise}
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where \(\Omega(\cdot)\) denotes a projection function that extracts the goal-relevant components from the state or goal state. A reward of 1 is provided when the Euclidean distance between \(\Omega(s_{t+1)}\)

